    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-04-11T12:52:36Z",
    "comment_count": 3,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There currently isn't. The best alternative is emulating `<C-g><C-n>...<C-n>` necessary number of times. Which is suboptimal, yes.\r\n\r\nAs this is a second (pretty valid) use case for adding similar functionality in a span of a week, I'll think about it a bit more. It will probably be something like `set_picker_matches(opts)` with `opts.current_ind` and `opts.marked_inds`. *Or* a second argument to `set_picker_match_inds()` that would allow setting indexes for matches (as is currently), \"current\", and \"marked\". I'll take a closer look.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">There currently isn't. The best alternative is emulating <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-g&gt;&lt;C-n&gt;...&lt;C-n&gt;</code> necessary number of times. Which is suboptimal, yes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As this is a second (pretty valid) use case for adding similar functionality in a span of a week, I'll think about it a bit more. It will probably be something like <code class=\"notranslate\">set_picker_matches(opts)</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">opts.current_ind</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">opts.marked_inds</code>. <em>Or</em> a second argument to <code class=\"notranslate\">set_picker_match_inds()</code> that would allow setting indexes for matches (as is currently), \"current\", and \"marked\". I'll take a closer look.</p>",
            "bodyText": "There currently isn't. The best alternative is emulating <C-g><C-n>...<C-n> necessary number of times. Which is suboptimal, yes.\nAs this is a second (pretty valid) use case for adding similar functionality in a span of a week, I'll think about it a bit more. It will probably be something like set_picker_matches(opts) with opts.current_ind and opts.marked_inds. Or a second argument to set_picker_match_inds() that would allow setting indexes for matches (as is currently), \"current\", and \"marked\". I'll take a closer look.",
