            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I would also like to have this.\r\n\r\nPerhaps also relevant: [discussion goto alternate](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/906#discussioncomment-9537899).\r\n\r\nYou ask if there is a way to set the current index. I think there is, but it is not trivial.\r\nI am doing something similar in my internal [pick_hinted](https://github.com/abeldekat/nvim_pde/blob/70d6b7e6043807e2503adf4ae3ce4761eeeeac30/lua/ak/mini/pick_hinted.lua#L156) plugin, discussed [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/1109).\r\n\r\nIn the code, I am using the `MiniPickStart` event to setup the plugin, decorating the match and show functions for `MiniPick.set_picker_opts`. Now, each picker can opt in to also display hints. Internally, I move the chosen hinted item to the top of `get_picker_matches.all_inds`.\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I would also like to have this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Perhaps also relevant: <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/906#discussioncomment-9537899\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/906/hovercard?comment_id=9537899\">discussion goto alternate</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You ask if there is a way to set the current index. I think there is, but it is not trivial.<br>\nI am doing something similar in my internal <a href=\"https://github.com/abeldekat/nvim_pde/blob/70d6b7e6043807e2503adf4ae3ce4761eeeeac30/lua/ak/mini/pick_hinted.lua#L156\">pick_hinted</a> plugin, discussed <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/1109\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1109/hovercard\">here</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In the code, I am using the <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPickStart</code> event to setup the plugin, decorating the match and show functions for <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.set_picker_opts</code>. Now, each picker can opt in to also display hints. Internally, I move the chosen hinted item to the top of <code class=\"notranslate\">get_picker_matches.all_inds</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "I would also like to have this.\nPerhaps also relevant: discussion goto alternate.\nYou ask if there is a way to set the current index. I think there is, but it is not trivial.\nI am doing something similar in my internal pick_hinted plugin, discussed here.\nIn the code, I am using the MiniPickStart event to setup the plugin, decorating the match and show functions for MiniPick.set_picker_opts. Now, each picker can opt in to also display hints. Internally, I move the chosen hinted item to the top of get_picker_matches.all_inds.",
