        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is now possible on latest `main` with [`MiniPick.set_picker_match_inds({ ind }, 'current')`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/bddfbfc4c1dbca6b852f512e554cf2e05c2960a8/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1386-L1387).\r\n\r\nA more appropriate name now would have been `set_picker_inds`, but decided to not introduce another breaking change (there is already a lot in the current release).\r\n\r\nHope this will help making some interesting picker behavior a bit easier.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This is now possible on latest <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code> with <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/bddfbfc4c1dbca6b852f512e554cf2e05c2960a8/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1386-L1387\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.set_picker_match_inds({ ind }, 'current')</code></a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A more appropriate name now would have been <code class=\"notranslate\">set_picker_inds</code>, but decided to not introduce another breaking change (there is already a lot in the current release).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hope this will help making some interesting picker behavior a bit easier.</p>",
            "bodyText": "This is now possible on latest main with MiniPick.set_picker_match_inds({ ind }, 'current').\nA more appropriate name now would have been set_picker_inds, but decided to not introduce another breaking change (there is already a lot in the current release).\nHope this will help making some interesting picker behavior a bit easier.",
